From: Deco X55 v3 OpenWrt port
Subject: batman-adv: shorten the bridge loop avoidance period to 1 s

With a wired backhaul, a satellite and the main node sit on the same LAN and become BLA
backbone gateways for each other. When the satellite's cable is pulled, the main node keeps it
as a backbone gateway until BATADV_BLA_BACKBONE_TIMEOUT (6 periods) expires and, until then,
drops the satellite's frames arriving over the wireless mesh (they "should" come from the LAN).
With the stock 10 s period that is 60-70 s without connectivity. A 1 s period gives ~6-7 s.
Cost: one small announcement frame per backbone gateway and VLAN per second on the LAN.
Claims time out after 10 s instead of 100 s and are re-learnt from the next frame.
The loop detection interval (6 periods = 6 s) stays above its 3 s timeout.

--- a/net/batman-adv/main.h
+++ b/net/batman-adv/main.h
@@ -104,7 +104,7 @@
 #define BATADV_MAX_AGGREGATION_BYTES 512
 #define BATADV_MAX_AGGREGATION_MS 100
 
-#define BATADV_BLA_PERIOD_LENGTH	10000	/* 10 seconds */
+#define BATADV_BLA_PERIOD_LENGTH	1000	/* 1 second (Deco X55 port: fast wired-backhaul failover) */
 #define BATADV_BLA_BACKBONE_TIMEOUT	(BATADV_BLA_PERIOD_LENGTH * 6)
 #define BATADV_BLA_CLAIM_TIMEOUT	(BATADV_BLA_PERIOD_LENGTH * 10)
 #define BATADV_BLA_WAIT_PERIODS		3
